## Allowlist spec (user-defined)

### Storage format

Store user entries in `chrome.storage.sync` (or local if you want privacy-only):

* `example.com` (matches exact host + subdomains if you choose)
* `*.example.com` (explicit wildcard)
* `sub.example.com` (exact)

### Matching rules (recommendation)

* Normalize host to punycode + lowercase
* If allowlist contains:

  * `example.com`: match `example.com` and `*.example.com` (user-friendly)
  * `*.example.com`: match subdomains only, not apex (optional)
* Never allowlist by full URL path initially; keep it domain-based to stay simple.

