## Test plan (you’ll thank yourself later)

### Positive tests (should block/warn)

* Fake ClickFix pages that copy:

  * `powershell -enc ...`
  * `curl http://... | sh`
  * `mshta http://...`
  * payloads with RLO/zero-width chars
* Pages that copy on load or mouseover (strict should block)

### Negative tests (should not break)

* Copy buttons on GitHub, docs sites, password managers, 2FA sites
* Copy of normal URLs, UUIDs, invite codes, JSON snippets
* Ctrl/Cmd+C on selected text

### Regression tests

* Multiple frames/iframes
* SPA navigation (URL changes without reload)
* sites with heavy JS that redefine clipboard APIs

